{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2914","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2914","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2914\",\"parent_revision\":\"03ca20d41b9c943b413b49956d679b398aa3deb8\",\"root_revision\":\"037066d63464b1e34ab3f7c571b3e224cd09e985b2cf92eb94b7c81ce0a767c6\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: Ideas\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-16\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nDiscovered while fixing the stale-mutation-clobber bug in PR #2906 (commit 303b2319) \u2014 explicitly left out of scope there. list_content's online branch calls self._cache.cache_content(record) for every discovered record without dequeuing any matching pending mutation, same shape as the bug just fixed in put_content's direct-write success path. Not yet confirmed as a live reproducible bug (list_content is a bulk discovery read, not a caller-intended write, so the exposure window may differ) \u2014 needs investigation to confirm whether a stale pending mutation can still clobber a list_content-cached record on a later replay, and if so whether the same dequeue-on-fresh-write fix applies or whether list_content's bulk nature needs a different treatment.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Not specified\\n- **Priority**: Ideas\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-16\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **bug(backlog-mcp): list_content's bulk discovery read caches records without touching pending queue, same footgun class as put_content** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"1422c9255ff1502cb7360c3bb5566cc4d9682630f442cc9f022d232eb266c2c5\",\"commen